Qwen3.8-27B on TensorFold v0.6.2 (56e2e3e): a pinned attention-cache pool for the concurrent decoder (one GPU).
TENSORFOLD_KV_POOL_GIB=80 reserves that much cache memory once startup is done (one block, touched so its pages are real,
freed into torch's allocator and never released: the decoder's cache-trimming calls become no-ops). The streams' caches and
the kept prompt states grow inside it; the memory gate counts what torch holds beyond the weights and fixed buffers
against the pool instead of asking the host's free memory. The startup estimate counts the pool instead of caches that grow.
Unset, nothing changes. Applies after 0004.

